      "title": "About this workflow",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Fine-tune a LoRA on your shot\n\nGive the model a few correct mattes of a hard shot and it learns that shot as a small LoRA (rank 8, about 2M parameters). About 1 s per step on an RTX 4090 at the largest crop.\n\n- **target_alpha**: correct mattes, white = subject (rotoscoped or cleaned-up keys). One per frame, or a few frames listed in `target_frames`, e.g. `0, 24, 48`.\n- **save_name**: saves to `models/corridorkey2/loras`; load it later with the LoRA node's `lora_name`.\n- The `info` output reports a check loss on the same crops before and after training.\n\nFine-Tune (Advanced) adds the scope, rank, learning rate, window, crop, every loss weight (alpha, Laplacian, gradient, composition, foreground, temporal, deep supervision) and the hint curriculum.\n\n**Your footage:** replace **Demo Clip** with **Load Video → Get Video Components** (or an image sequence loader) and connect its `images`. The Demo Clip is a synthetic green-screen shot with its exact matte, so every example runs without media.\n\nLoRAs are adaptations of CorridorKey 2.0 and fall under its licence."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Fine-tune a LoRA on your shot\n\nGive the model a few correct mattes of a hard shot and it learns that shot as a small LoRA (rank 8, about 2M parameters). About 1 s per step on an RTX 4090 at the largest crop.\n\n- **target_alpha**: correct mattes, white = subject (rotoscoped or cleaned-up keys). One per frame, or a few frames listed in `target_frames`, e.g. `0, 24, 48`.\n- **save_name**: saves to `models/corridorkey2/loras`; load it later with the LoRA node's `lora_name`.\n- The `info` output reports a check loss on the same crops before and after training.\n\nFine-Tune (Advanced) adds the scope, rank, learning rate, window, crop, every loss weight (alpha, Laplacian, gradient, composition, foreground, temporal, deep supervision) and the hint curriculum.\n\n**Your footage:** replace **Demo Clip** with **Load Video → Get Video Components** (or an image sequence loader) and connect its `images`. The Demo Clip is a synthetic green-screen shot with its exact matte, so every example runs without media.\n\nLoRAs are adaptations of CorridorKey 2.0 and fall under its licence."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
